GableLBM Licensing
==================

Copyright (c) 2025-2026 FutureBuild AI and contributors.

GableLBM is free software, offered under a conditional dual license built
from two standard GNU licenses. Which grant applies depends on how you
deploy it:

1. SINGLE-DEALER DEPLOYMENT — GNU GPL v3.0 or later
   If you deploy GableLBM (modified or not) to operate the lumber/building-
   materials business of a single dealer organization — one legal entity,
   together with its majority-owned affiliates, running the software for its
   own operations, including serving its own customers, staff, drivers, and
   suppliers through the software's portals — your license is the GNU
   General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version.
   See LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt.

2. MULTI-DEALER OPERATION — GNU AGPL v3.0 or later
   If you deploy, host, offer, or customize GableLBM (modified or not) for
   use by or on behalf of more than one dealer organization — including
   operating it as a service for other companies or brands, reselling a
   customized version to multiple dealers, or running a shared instance for
   a buying group or co-op's member dealers — your license is the GNU Affero
   General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version.
   See LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt.

In SPDX terms: GPL-3.0-or-later OR AGPL-3.0-or-later, where the applicable
grant is determined by the deployment conditions above rather than by the
licensee's free choice.

Plain-language intent (not a substitute for the license texts): a dealer
running GableLBM for its own business takes it under the GPL and owes
nobody source code for merely hosting it. An integrator, vendor, or group
serving multiple dealer organizations takes it under the AGPL, so the
dealers and users they serve are entitled to the source of the version
being run — improvements made at the ecosystem level flow back to the
ecosystem.

Contributions are accepted under the same terms (see CONTRIBUTING.md):
by contributing, you license your contribution under both GPL-3.0-or-later
and AGPL-3.0-or-later so the project can extend both grants above.

Both full license texts are in the LICENSES/ directory and form part of
this distribution. If your intended use does not fit either condition
cleanly, contact FutureBuild AI (colton@futurebuild.ai) before deploying.
